				<register>
					<dim>8</dim>
					<dimIncrement>4</dimIncrement>
					<name>LPCR[%s]</name>
					<description>Port 13 LVDS Pad Control Register 0
 resetvalue={:0x5480,:0x54C0,After SSW execution:0x54E0,After SSW execution:0x5480}</description>
					<addressOffset>160</addressOffset>
					<size>32</size>
					<resetValue>0</resetValue>
					<resetMask>4294901760</resetMask>
					<fields>
						<field>
							<name>PS</name>
							<description>Pad Supply Selection. Selects between 5V or 3.3V supply on V EXT for the pad pair. Used in RX and TX pads  Driven to LVDS pad control   8220 LVDS 5EN  8221 . Needs also be connected to the        related bias distributor.</description>
							<lsb>7</lsb>
							<msb>7</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>TEN_CTRL</name>
							<description>LVDS TX EN controller. The LVDS TX EN control function can be selected from the Port  default         or HSCT module  where this is connected .</description>
							<lsb>8</lsb>
							<msb>8</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>TX_EN</name>
							<description>Enable Transmit LVDS. Enable the transmit LVDS   disable CMOS path. If this bit is set to 0          no transfer on LVDS data path can be initiated and the LVDS driver is        disabled  powered down . Driven to LVDS pad control   8220 LVDSEN  8221 .</description>
							<lsb>9</lsb>
							<msb>9</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>VDIFFADJ</name>
							<description>LVDS Output Amplitude Tuning. With these two configuration bits the LVDS output current amplitude can        be adjusted. The voltage swing depending on VDIFFADJ setting is        documented in the Data Sheet  see parameter V OD . Driven to LVDS pad controls LVDS VDIFF ADJ 1 0 .</description>
							<lsb>10</lsb>
							<msb>11</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>VOSDYN</name>
							<description>Tune Bit of VOS Control Loop Static Dynamic. Tune bit to change V OS control loop        between static and dynamic mode. Don  8217 t change reset value.</description>
							<lsb>12</lsb>
							<msb>12</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>VOSEXT</name>
							<description>Tune Bit of VOS Control Loop Internal External. Tune bit to change V OS control loop. Tune bit to change the measurement point of the V OS control loop between the actual LVDS signal on PADP PADN or the internal        replica. Effective only if control loop is set to static mode with        VOSDYN   0. Don  8217 t change reset value.</description>
							<lsb>13</lsb>
							<msb>13</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>TX_PD</name>
							<description>LVDS Power Down. Unused in this device. LVDS disabled by TX EN means power down. According to LVDS design spec in C40 power down means LVDSEN 0. So in        C40 this bit is obsolete.</description>
							<lsb>14</lsb>
							<msb>14</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>TX_PWDPD</name>
							<description>Enable TX Power down pull down.. This function disables or enables the LVDS pull down resistor. The        application code must disable TX power down pull down resistor with a        power up. With a LVDS Power Down configuration the pull down function        must be enabled  if required. Driven to LVDS pad control   8220 LVDS PDN  8221 .</description>
