								<description>Configuration flag x  x 0 2  for alarm 31 belonging to alarm group i.   CF31. The configuration flags 0  1 and 2 must be used together to define the        behavior of the SMU core when a fault state is reported by the alarm n        belonging to this group.</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>0</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>CF1</name>
								<description>Configuration flag x  x 0 2  for alarm 31 belonging to alarm group i.   CF31. The configuration flags 0  1 and 2 must be used together to define the        behavior of the SMU core when a fault state is reported by the alarm n        belonging to this group.</description>
								<lsb>1</lsb>
