						<field>
							<name>CC61ST</name>
							<description>Capture Compare State Bits for CC62  x   0  1  2    CC62ST. Bits CC6xST monitor the state of the capture compare channels. Bits        CC6xST  x  160    160 0  1  2  are related to T12 and are set and cleared        according to the T12 switching rules.</description>
							<lsb>1</lsb>
							<msb>1</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CC62ST</name>
							<description>Capture Compare State Bits for CC62  x   0  1  2    CC62ST. Bits CC6xST monitor the state of the capture compare channels. Bits        CC6xST  x  160    160 0  1  2  are related to T12 and are set and cleared        according to the T12 switching rules.</description>
							<lsb>2</lsb>
							<msb>2</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CCPOS60</name>
							<description>Sampled Hall Pattern Bits   CCPOS62. Bits CCPOS6x  x   0  1  2  are indicating the value of the input Hall pattern that has been compared to the current and expected value. The value is sampled when the event HCRDY  Hall Compare Ready  occurs.</description>
							<lsb>3</lsb>
							<msb>3</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CCPOS61</name>
							<description>Sampled Hall Pattern Bits   CCPOS62. Bits CCPOS6x  x   0  1  2  are indicating the value of the input Hall pattern that has been compared to the current and expected value. The value is sampled when the event HCRDY  Hall Compare Ready  occurs.</description>
							<lsb>4</lsb>
							<msb>4</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CCPOS62</name>
							<description>Sampled Hall Pattern Bits   CCPOS62. Bits CCPOS6x  x   0  1  2  are indicating the value of the input Hall pattern that has been compared to the current and expected value. The value is sampled when the event HCRDY  Hall Compare Ready  occurs.</description>
							<lsb>5</lsb>
							<msb>5</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CC63ST</name>
							<description>Capture Compare State Bit for CC63   CC63ST. Bit CC63ST monitors the state of the compare channel. Bit CC63ST is related to T13 and is set and cleared according to the T13 switching rules.</description>
							<lsb>6</lsb>
							<msb>6</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CC60PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs CC62  x   0  1  2    CC62PS. Bits CC6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits CC6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>8</lsb>
							<msb>8</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CC61PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs CC62  x   0  1  2    CC62PS. Bits CC6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits CC6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>10</lsb>
							<msb>10</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>CC62PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs CC62  x   0  1  2    CC62PS. Bits CC6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits CC6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>12</lsb>
							<msb>12</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>COUT60PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs COUT62  x   0  1  2    COUT62PS. Bits COUT6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits COUT6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>9</lsb>
							<msb>9</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>COUT61PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs COUT62  x   0  1  2    COUT62PS. Bits COUT6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits COUT6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>11</lsb>
							<msb>11</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>COUT62PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Outputs COUT62  x   0  1  2    COUT62PS. Bits COUT6xPS select the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bits COUT6xPS  x   0  1  2  are related to T12. In capture mode  these bits are not used.</description>
							<lsb>13</lsb>
							<msb>13</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>COUT63PS</name>
							<description>Passive State Select for Compare Output COUT63   COUT63PS. Bit COUT63PS selects the state of the corresponding compare channel  that is considered to be the passive state. During the passive state  the passive level  defined in register PSLR  is driven by the output pin. Bit COUT63PS is related to T13.</description>
							<lsb>14</lsb>
							<msb>14</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>T13IM</name>
							<description>T13 Inverted Modulation   T13IM. Bit T13IM inverts the T13 signal for the modulation of the CC6x and COUT6x  x   0  1  2  signals.</description>
							<lsb>15</lsb>
							<msb>15</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
					</fields>
				</register>
				<register>
					<name>CMPMODIF</name>
					<description>Compare State Modification Register
 resetvalue={Application Reset:0x0}</description>
					<addressOffset>100</addressOffset>
					<size>32</size>
					<resetValue>0</resetValue>
					<resetMask>4294967295</resetMask>
					<fields>
						<field>
							<name>MCC60S</name>
							<description>Capture Compare Status Modification Bits MCC62S  x   0  1  2    MCC62S. These bits are used to set the corresponding bits CC6xST by SW. The functionality of a write access to bits concerning the same        capture compare state bit is shown in CROSSREFERENCE .</description>
							<lsb>0</lsb>
							<msb>0</msb>
							<access>write-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>MCC61S</name>
							<description>Capture Compare Status Modification Bits MCC62S  x   0  1  2    MCC62S. These bits are used to set the corresponding bits CC6xST by SW. The functionality of a write access to bits concerning the same        capture compare state bit is shown in CROSSREFERENCE .</description>
							<lsb>1</lsb>
							<msb>1</msb>
							<access>write-only</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>MCC62S</name>
							<description>Capture Compare Status Modification Bits MCC62S  x   0  1  2    MCC62S. These bits are used to set the corresponding bits CC6xST by SW. The functionality of a write access to bits concerning the same        capture compare state bit is shown in CROSSREFERENCE .</description>
							<lsb>2</lsb>
