								<name>BRG_MODE</name>
								<description>Defines the operation mode for the AEI bridge. Reset value depends on the hardware configuration chosen by silicon vendor. BRG MODE shall  not be written with 0.</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>0</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>MSK_WR_RSP</name>
								<description>Mask write response. With active write buffer MSK WR RSP 1  execution of actions can be        delayed due to previous inserted write actions in the transaction buffer        which wait to be serviced. This can lead to the fact that an access on        the bus to a different peripheral than the GTM might be executed earlier        in time than the write access buffered in the GTM. Applications must be        setup up with this in mind otherwise unexpected operation can happen.</description>
								<lsb>1</lsb>
								<msb>1</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
