					<register>
						<name>TIMi_RST</name>
						<description>TIM0 Global Software Reset Register
 resetvalue={Application Reset:0x0}</description>
						<addressOffset>124</addressOffset>
						<size>32</size>
						<resetValue>0</resetValue>
						<resetMask>4294967295</resetMask>
						<fields>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH0</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>0</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH1</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>1</lsb>
								<msb>1</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH2</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>2</lsb>
								<msb>2</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH3</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>3</lsb>
								<msb>3</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH4</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>4</lsb>
								<msb>4</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH5</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>5</lsb>
								<msb>5</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH6</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
								<lsb>6</lsb>
								<msb>6</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RST_CH7</name>
								<description>Software reset of channel 7. This bit is cleared automatically after write by CPU. The channel        registers are set to their reset values and channel operation is stopped        immediately. Please note  that the RST field width of this register depends on the        number of implemented channels m within this sub module. This register        description represents a register layout for m   8.</description>
