								<lsb>10</lsb>
								<msb>10</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>AEN3</name>
								<description>ACTION 7 enable. This bit can be written only if the correspondent WADx bit is set in          the same access. It can be set for debug purposes by CPU also  when          DPLL is disabled. The enable bit becomes active only when the DPLL is          in operation  DEN 1 . For WADi  1  only the corresponding AENi bits are writable. The AENi          bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADi 0.</description>
								<lsb>11</lsb>
								<msb>11</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>AEN4</name>
								<description>ACTION 7 enable. This bit can be written only if the correspondent WADx bit is set in          the same access. It can be set for debug purposes by CPU also  when          DPLL is disabled. The enable bit becomes active only when the DPLL is          in operation  DEN 1 . For WADi  1  only the corresponding AENi bits are writable. The AENi          bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADi 0.</description>
								<lsb>12</lsb>
								<msb>12</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>AEN5</name>
								<description>ACTION 7 enable. This bit can be written only if the correspondent WADx bit is set in          the same access. It can be set for debug purposes by CPU also  when          DPLL is disabled. The enable bit becomes active only when the DPLL is          in operation  DEN 1 . For WADi  1  only the corresponding AENi bits are writable. The AENi          bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADi 0.</description>
								<lsb>13</lsb>
								<msb>13</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>AEN6</name>
								<description>ACTION 7 enable. This bit can be written only if the correspondent WADx bit is set in          the same access. It can be set for debug purposes by CPU also  when          DPLL is disabled. The enable bit becomes active only when the DPLL is          in operation  DEN 1 . For WADi  1  only the corresponding AENi bits are writable. The AENi          bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADi 0.</description>
								<lsb>14</lsb>
								<msb>14</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>AEN7</name>
								<description>ACTION 7 enable. This bit can be written only if the correspondent WADx bit is set in          the same access. It can be set for debug purposes by CPU also  when          DPLL is disabled. The enable bit becomes active only when the DPLL is          in operation  DEN 1 . For WADi  1  only the corresponding AENi bits are writable. The AENi          bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADi 0.</description>
								<lsb>15</lsb>
								<msb>15</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>WAD0</name>
								<description>Write control bit of Action 7. For WADx  1  only the corresponding AENx bits are writable. The AENx        bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADx 0.</description>
								<lsb>16</lsb>
								<msb>16</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>WAD1</name>
								<description>Write control bit of Action 7. For WADx  1  only the corresponding AENx bits are writable. The AENx        bits remain unchanged when the corresponding WADx 0.</description>
