								<description>RAM regions 1a  1b and 2 are to be initialized. Setting the INIT RAM bit results only in a RAM reset when the DPLL is        not enabled  DEN 0 . Depending on the vendor configuration  the connected RAM regions are        initialized to zero in the case of a module HW reset or for setting the        RST bit in the GTM RST register. In the case of no RAM initialization  it must be ensured that all        relevant parameters are configured correctly. Otherwise  there is no        guarantee to get a predictable behavior.</description>
