						<addressOffset>1056</addressOffset>
						<size>32</size>
						<resetValue>0</resetValue>
						<resetMask>0</resetMask>
						<fields>
							<field>
								<name>THMI</name>
								<description>Minimal time between active and inactive TRIGGER slope  uint16 . The time value corresponds to the time stamp clock counts  this does mean the clock selected for the TBU CH0 BASE  see TBU CH0 CTRL        register  set min. value  generate the TINI interrupt in the case of a violation        for THMI gt 0. Typical retention time values after an active slope can be e.g. between        45   181 s  forwards  and 90   181 s  backwards . When THMI is zero  consider        always a THMI violation  forwards .</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>15</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
