								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TB12_SEL</name>
								<description>Select time base value TBU TS1 or TBU TS2. This bit is only applicable if three time bases are present in the GTM.        Otherwise  this bit is reserved.</description>
								<lsb>2</lsb>
								<msb>2</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ARU_EN</name>
								<description>ARU Input stream enable</description>
								<lsb>3</lsb>
								<msb>3</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ACB_1_0</name>
								<description>Signal level control bits. Note  These bits are only applicable if ARU EN   0.</description>
								<lsb>4</lsb>
								<msb>5</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ACB_4_3_2</name>
								<description>ATOM SOMB compare strategy. These bits are only applicable if ARU EN   0.</description>
								<lsb>6</lsb>
								<msb>8</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>CMP_CTRL</name>
								<description>CCUx compare strategy select. The compare unit CCU0 or CCU1 that compares against TBU TS0  depending        on CCUx control mode defined by ACB CM 4 2   always performs a        greater equal comparison  independent of the CMP CTRL bit.</description>
								<lsb>9</lsb>
								<msb>9</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>EUPM</name>
								<description>Extended update mode. If EUPM 1 and after a CCU0 compare match  if ARU EN 0  written CM0 value not stored. if ARU EN 1  ARU read request is continued and CM1 is updated until CCU1        compare match. Received CM0 is not stored. This bit is only applicable in SOMC and SOMB mode.</description>
								<lsb>10</lsb>
								<msb>10</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>SL</name>
								<description>Initial signal level after channel enable. Reset value depends on the hardware configuration chosen by silicon        vendor. If the output is disabled  the output ATOM OUT x  is set to inverse        value of SL. If FREEZE 0  the following note is valid  If the channel is disabled  the output register of SOU unit is set to        value of SL. If FREEZE 1  the following note is valid  If the channel is disabled  the output register of SOU unit is not        changed  and output ATOM OUT x  is not changed.</description>
								<lsb>11</lsb>
								<msb>11</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>WR_REQ</name>
								<description>CPU Write request bit for late compare register update. The CPU can disable subsequent ARU read requests by the channel and can        update the shadow registers with new compare values  while the compare        units operate on old compare values received by former ARU accesses  if        occurred. On a compare match event  the WR REQ bit will be reset by hardware. At the point of the force update  only the shadow registers SR0 and SR1        are transferred into the CM0  CM1 registers. The output action is still        defined by the ACBI bit field described by the ARU together with the old        compare values for CM0 CM1.</description>
								<lsb>16</lsb>
								<msb>16</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>EXTTRIGOUT</name>
								<description>TIM EXT CAPTURE x  as potential output signal TRIG  x </description>
								<lsb>23</lsb>
								<msb>23</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TRIGOUT</name>
								<description>Trigger output selection  output signal TRIG CHx  of module ATOM CHx</description>
								<lsb>24</lsb>
								<msb>24</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ABM</name>
								<description>ARU blocking mode</description>
								<lsb>27</lsb>
								<msb>27</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>SOMB</name>
								<description>SOMB  SOMB mode</description>
								<lsb>30</lsb>
								<msb>30</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>FREEZE</name>
								<description>FREEZE</description>
								<lsb>31</lsb>
								<msb>31</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
					</register>
					<register>
						<name>CH1_SOMC</name>
						<description>ATOM0 Channel 7 Control Register in SOMC Mode
 resetvalue={Application Reset:0x0800,Application Reset:0x0,Application Reset:0x0,Application Reset:0x0,Application Reset:0x0,Application Reset:0x0}</description>
						<addressOffset>132</addressOffset>
						<size>32</size>
						<resetValue>0</resetValue>
						<resetMask>4294965247</resetMask>
						<fields>
							<field>
								<name>MODE</name>
								<description>ATOM channel mode select</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>1</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TB12_SEL</name>
								<description>Select time base value TBU TS1 or TBU TS2. This bit is only applicable if three time bases are present in the GTM.        Otherwise  this bit is reserved.</description>
								<lsb>2</lsb>
								<msb>2</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ARU_EN</name>
								<description>ARU Input stream enable</description>
								<lsb>3</lsb>
								<msb>3</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ACB_1_0</name>
								<description>Signal level control bits. These bits are only applicable if ARU EN   0.</description>
								<lsb>4</lsb>
								<msb>5</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ACB_4_3_2</name>
								<description>ATOM control bits ACB 4   ACB 3   ACB 2 . Independent of ARU EN  a writing of 0b111 cancels any pending CCU0 or        CCU1 compare. Note  These bits are defining the compare strategy only if        ARU EN   0.</description>
								<lsb>6</lsb>
								<msb>8</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>CMP_CTRL</name>
								<description>CCUx compare strategy select. The compare unit CCU0 or CCU1 that compares against TBU TS0  depending        on CCUx control mode defined by ACBI 4 2  or ACB42  always performs a        greater equal comparison  independent on CMP CTRL bit.</description>
								<lsb>9</lsb>
								<msb>9</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>EUPM</name>
								<description>Extended Update Mode. If EUPM 1 and after a CCU0 compare match  If ARU EN 0  written CM0 value not stored. If ARU EN 1  ARU read request is continued and CM1 is updated until CCU1        compare match. Received CM0 values are not stored. This bit is only applicable in SOMC and SOMB mode.</description>
								<lsb>10</lsb>
								<msb>10</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>SL</name>
								<description>Initial signal level after channel enable. Reset value depends on the hardware configuration chosen by silicon        vendor. If the output is disabled  the output ATOM OUT x  is set to inverse        value of SL. If FREEZE 0  following note is valid  If the channel is disabled  the output register of SOU unit is set to        value of SL. If FREEZE 1  following note is valid  If the channel is disabled  the output register of SOU unit is not        changed  and output ATOM OUT x  is not changed.</description>
								<lsb>11</lsb>
								<msb>11</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>WR_REQ</name>
								<description>CPU write request bit. The CPU can disable subsequent ARU read requests by the channel and can        update the shadow registers with new compare values  while the compare        units operate on old compare values received by former ARU accesses  if        occurred. On a compare match event  the WR REQ bit will be reset by hardware. At the point of the force update  only the shadow registers SR0 and SR1        are transferred into the CM0  CM1 registers. The output action is still        defined by the ACBI bit field described by the ARU together with the old        compare values for CM0 CM1.</description>
								<lsb>16</lsb>
								<msb>16</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>EXTTRIGOUT</name>
								<description>Select TIM EXT CAPTURE x  as potential output signal TRIG  x </description>
								<lsb>23</lsb>
								<msb>23</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TRIGOUT</name>
								<description>TRIGOUT  Trigger output selection  output signal TRIG CHx  of module ATOM CHx</description>
								<lsb>24</lsb>
								<msb>24</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>SLA</name>
								<description>Serve last ARU communication strategy. Please note  that setting of this bit has only effect  when ACBI 4 2  is        configured for serve last compare strategy   quot 100 quot    quot 101 quot   or  quot 110 quot  . When this bit is not set  the captured time stamps in the shadow        registers SRx are only provided after the CCU1 match occurred. The        ACBO 4 3  bits always return  quot 10 quot  in that case. By setting this bit  the ATOM channel also provides the captured time        stamps after the CCU0 match event to the ARU. The ACBO 4 3  bits are set        to   8220 01  8221  in that case. After the CCU1 match event  the time stamps are        captured again in the SRx registers and provided to the ARU. The        ACBO 4 3  bits are set to   8220 10  8221 . When the data in the shadow registers        after the CCU0 match was not consumed by an ARU destination and the CCU1        match occurs  the data in the shadow registers is overwritten by the new        captured time stamps. The ATOM channel does not request new data from        the ARU when the CCU0 match values are read from an ARU destination.</description>
								<lsb>25</lsb>
								<msb>25</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ABM</name>
								<description>ARU blocking mode</description>
								<lsb>27</lsb>
								<msb>27</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>FREEZE</name>
								<description>FREEZE</description>
								<lsb>31</lsb>
								<msb>31</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
					</register>
