							<field>
								<name>MCS_IRQ</name>
								<description>Interrupt request by MCS channel x. This bit will be cleared on a CPU write access with a value of  1 . A          read access leaves the bit unchanged. By writing a  1  to this register  the IRQ flag in the MCS channel          status register STA is cleared.</description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>0</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>STK_ERR_IRQ</name>
								<description>Stack counter overflow underflow of channel x. Note  This bit will be cleared on a CPU write access with a value of  1 . A read access leaves the bit unchanged.</description>
								<lsb>1</lsb>
								<msb>1</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ERR_IRQ</name>
								<description>MCS channel x ERR interrupt. If the ERR bit of register STA is triggered  the ERR IRQ will also be          set. This bit will be cleared on a CPU write access with a value of  1 . A          read access leaves the bit unchanged.</description>
								<lsb>2</lsb>
								<msb>2</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
