						<field>
							<name>CMP0IR</name>
							<description>Compare Register CMP0 Interrupt Request Flag   CMP0IR. This bit indicates whether or not a compare match event of compare register CMP0 has occured. CMP0IR can be cleared by software and can be set by software  too  see ISCR register . After a STM reset operation  CMP0IR is immediately set as a result of a compare match event with the reset values of the STM and the compare registers CMP0. This flag does not gate the interrupt generation. i.e.  even if this flag is not cleared  compare match event interrupts are forwarded if CMPxEN is set.</description>
							<lsb>1</lsb>
							<msb>1</msb>
