					<fields>
						<field>
							<name>RST</name>
							<description>Kernel Reset   RST. This reset bit can be used to request for a kernel reset. The kernel reset will be executed if the reset bits of both kernel registers are set. The RST bit will be cleared  reset to 0   b after the kernel reset was executed.</description>
							<lsb>0</lsb>
							<msb>0</msb>
							<access>read-write</access>
						</field>
						<field>
							<name>RSTSTAT</name>
							<description>Kernel Reset Status   RSTSTAT. This bit indicates whether a kernel reset was executed or not. This bit is set after the execution of a kernel reset in the same clock cycle both reset bits. This bit can be cleared by writing with  1  to the CLR bit in the related KRSTCLR register.</description>
							<lsb>1</lsb>
							<msb>1</msb>
							<access>read-only</access>
						</field>
					</fields>
