								<lsb>4</lsb>
								<msb>7</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RxF0F</name>
								<description>IR.RF0F   RxF0F. Receive FIFO0 full interrupt assigned to an interrupt node</description>
								<lsb>8</lsb>
								<msb>11</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RxF1N</name>
								<description>IR.RF1N   RxF1N. Receive FIFO1 new message assigned to an interrupt node</description>
								<lsb>12</lsb>
								<msb>15</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RxF0N</name>
								<description>IR.RF0N   RxF0N. Receive FIFO0 new message assigned to an interrupt node</description>
								<lsb>16</lsb>
								<msb>19</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>RETI</name>
								<description>Receive Timeouts   RETI. can be assigned here. IR.TOO  time out event  and TE  Timer Event </description>
								<lsb>20</lsb>
								<msb>23</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TRAQ</name>
								<description>Transmission Queue Events   TRAQ. can be assigned here. IR.TFE Transmission FIFO Empty</description>
								<lsb>24</lsb>
								<msb>27</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TRACO</name>
								<description>Interrupts of the transmission control   TRACO. can be assigned here. IR.TCF  Transmission Cancellation Finished  and        IR.TF  Transmission Completed . As        an additional information the copy of a local time event is shown here        with TTIR.SWT  Stop Watch Event . Further on the TTIR.TTMI Trigger Time        Event Internal  TTIR.RTMI  Register Time Mark   TTIR.SOG  Start of Gap          TTIR.CSM  Change of Synchronization Mode   TTIR.SMC  Start Matrix Cycle         and TTIR.SBC  Start of Basic Cycle  are shown here.</description>
								<lsb>28</lsb>
								<msb>31</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
					</register>
					<register>
						<name>NPCRi</name>
						<description>Node 0 Port Control Register
 resetvalue={Application Reset:0x0}</description>
						<addressOffset>64</addressOffset>
						<size>32</size>
						<resetValue>0</resetValue>
						<resetMask>4294967295</resetMask>
						<fields>
							<field>
								<name>RXSEL</name>
								<description>Receive Select   RXSEL. RXSEL selects one out of 8 possible receive inputs. The CAN receive        signal is performed by the selected input.  see the device related        chapter for RXSEL </description>
								<lsb>0</lsb>
								<msb>2</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>LBM</name>
								<description>Loop Back Mode   LBM</description>
								<lsb>8</lsb>
								<msb>8</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>LOUT</name>
								<description>Loop Back Mode Out   LOUT. This bit is not implemented in TC39x A step silicon. The loop back bus is switched to the external CAN bus of the node.</description>
								<lsb>9</lsb>
								<msb>9</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>DELE</name>
								<description>Enable destructive read on ECR0.CEL   DELE. If this bit is set  the destructive read on ECRi.CEL and on the PSR        register takes place. Meaning  that with read access on ECRi  the CEL is        reset. The same is true for the PSR register  for the bits PXE  RFDF         RBRS  RESI  LEC and DLEC. After the destructive read it is advised to        reset the bit again.</description>
								<lsb>10</lsb>
								<msb>10</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
					</register>
					<register>
						<name>TTCRi</name>
						<description>Time Trigger Control Register
 resetvalue={Application Reset:0x0}</description>
						<addressOffset>240</addressOffset>
						<size>32</size>
						<resetValue>0</resetValue>
						<resetMask>4294967295</resetMask>
						<fields>
							<field>
								<name>ETESEL</name>
								<description>External Trigger Event Selection   ETESEL. This bit field defines the external trigger event that can be used to        trigger the transmission of the reference message. The event causes the        Event Trigger to be triggered. Control settings for this will not be        influenced.</description>
								<lsb>2</lsb>
								<msb>3</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>ETSSEL</name>
								<description>External Trigger Source Selection   ETSSEL. This bit fields selects the input source for the external reference        message trigger.</description>
								<lsb>4</lsb>
								<msb>6</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
							<field>
								<name>TTCTSS</name>
								<description>TTCapture Time Trigger Source Select   TTCTSS. This bit selects the input source for the TT Capture Time  TTCPT         trigger. This register influences the stop watch event trigger</description>
								<lsb>9</lsb>
								<msb>11</msb>
								<access>read-write</access>
							</field>
						</fields>
					</register>
